MISMATCHES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Attempt 2 (final): NONE. No pin mismatch, no device-class mismatch, no short,
  no open, no R-vs-X case (this design has no extracted resistor device -- the
  coil's R1 lives inside the black-boxed subckt on both sides).

  Attempt 1 (baseline, recorded because it is the reason attempt 2 exists):
  | # | Symptom | Diagnosis | Belongs to |
  |---|---------|-----------|------------|
  | 1 | Magic: 2x `Warning: Ports "B" and "A" are electrically shorted` | The coil | TOOLING |
  | 2 | `.subckt routed VDD Vcont Iref VSS` -- 4 ports, not 6 | short propagated into parent, fusing VDD+voutp+voutn | TOOLING |
  | 3 | netgen: voutn, voutp = "(no matching net)" | consequence of #2 | TOOLING |
  | 4 | netgen: C0, C1, DUMMY1 = "(no matching instance)" | consequence of #2 | TOOLING |
  | 5 | "Final result: Top level cell failed pin matching." | consequence of #2 | TOOLING |
  All five are ONE root cause: sky130A.tech has no `device` line for an inductor,
  so a drawn spiral extracts as plain wire and its two ports land on one node.
  This is NOT a layout connectivity bug. No layout geometry was changed to fix it.

